content.text:
Vance Oduya leans against the berth console, arms folded, and lets Mira work. The logs scroll past, mostly water-rationing chits and fuel tallies. Then one entry holds. A dock hand named in the margin saw the courier leave, and saw which way the courier went.

The timestamp is the problem. The entry is flagged for an inspection sweep at the next shift change, and whoever walks that ring will not leave the margin note standing.

Ren stands at the rail of the docking ring and watches the gantries. A cargo lifter idles at Berth Nine. Its pilot has not looked away from Mira's console once.

<npc>"You've found something,"</npc> Vance says. <npc>"Say it now, or I'll read it off your face."</npc>

