Vance's hands stay folded against his arm, then one slides to the console's edge. The thumb taps twice. Someone else has been watching Mira work, and Vance knows it.

You lean in the hatchway and watch those hands. His thumb drifts toward the purge key, the one that clears an entry before any sweep. He stops short and rests it flat.

"Well?" Vance says. The lifter's pilot has not looked away once.

